# gate baseline — per-case verdicts (verdict\tdescription). Regenerate with `cargo xtask gate --save`.
pass	a counter session bumps kv count on its kick-off message
pass	a handler serves two families but replies to only one; the caller resumes one effect and stays active on the other
pass	a handler's effect/reply payload round-trips to the caller, observed as e.payload on the effect-result
pass	a message carrying a multi-byte String payload round-trips to the receiver intact
pass	a message chains across three sessions a -> b -> c, each hop emitting to the next
pass	a message to an absent peer bounces a delivery-failure back to the sender, which folds it
pass	a reducer deletes KV slots and branches on the delete bool: true for a present key, false for an absent one
pass	a reducer prefix-scans a namespaced key range and counts exactly the in-prefix pairs
pass	a reducer reads an absent key (kv.get None) and a just-put key (kv.get Some) and witnesses both option arms
pass	a sender emits a message to a peer session, which the peer receives and folds
pass	a sender emits two messages to one peer in a single fold; the peer folds both in order
pass	a session stores a fixed mid-range byte value (decoder past the counter's 1)
pass	a session writes TWO kv keys on its kick-off (multi-key end-state)
pass	a worker performs a userspace effect served by a handler session, and resumes on the reply
pass	an effect no session serves is a permanent error that resumes the caller (no hang, no silent drop)
pass	an unanswered deferred effect leaves the caller active (blocked), the handler quiescent
pass	an unbounded effect/reply ping-pong is caught as a SettleUnbounded fault, not a hang
pass	one handler session serves two effect families; a caller performs both and resumes
pass	the effect correlation token is echoed to the caller on the effect-result (observed as e.resumes)
pass	the same counter IGNORES a non-message kick-off (else-branch writes no state)
pass	two sessions ping-pong: a emits to b, b replies to a, a folds the reply and stops
